      "body": "I suggest also dropping `bip-0375/deps/secp256k1lab` in this PR, with its README entry, and pointing its path in `test_runner.py` to `bip-0374/secp256k1lab/src`. I tried this locally and the 43 tests pass. The path change is needed: with the copy dropped and the path unchanged, importing `validator.inputs` before `deps.dleq` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'secp256k1lab'`.\n\nAt 503119d that copy is no longer used. `deps/dleq.py` loads `bip-0374/reference.py`, which puts `bip-0374/secp256k1lab/src` at the front of `sys.path`. This happens before the validator's first `secp256k1lab` import. So the validator already runs on BIP-374's copy, as `python3 -v bip-0375/test_runner.py` shows. The tests pass either way because the two copies are identical today. If they drift apart, no test will notice, and the README will still list the unused copy as a dependency.\n",
